        },
        {
          "id": 50622272,
          "author": "Nition",
          "publishedAt": "2026-11-24T01:27:45.000Z",
          "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50622272",
          "textZhHtml": "Is drum circle a business term here or does that mean literally that sat in a circle and played drums?"
        },
        {
          "id": 50623001,
          "author": "hydrox24",
          "publishedAt": "2026-11-24T02:54:58.000Z",
          "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50623001",
          "textZhHtml": "\"Beat the drum\" is a idiom which means enthusiastically speaking in support of an idea in order to persuade others to support it to.[^0]<p>Drum circle is a play on the idiom which implies there was a group of people \"Beating the drum\" together.</p><p>[0]: <a href=\"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/bang-beat-the-drum\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/bang-bea...</a></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": 50623396,
          "author": "cco",
          "publishedAt": "2026-11-24T03:47:21.000Z",
          "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50623396",
          "textZhHtml": "A drum circle is not a group of people \"banging the drum\", it has a kumbaya aspect to it, peaceful protest, a coming together etc."
        },
        {
          "id": 50625483,
          "author": "kbenson",
          "publishedAt": "2026-11-24T08:45:09.000Z",
          "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50625483",
          "textZhHtml": "Which is why it's a <i>play</i> on the idiom, meaning there's some variation or twist or pun, not direct equivalence. You're expected to put together what was explained, or at least intuit that's what they were going for, even if the exact linkage wasn't obvious."
        },
        {
          "id": 50627293,
          "author": "trollbridge",
          "publishedAt": "2026-11-24T12:35:43.000Z",
          "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50627293",
          "textZhHtml": "Or a drum circle is how a group of people prepare for war, including as part of a summoning ritual to arouse martial spirits."
        },
        {
          "id": 50626099,
          "author": "fartfeatures",
          "publishedAt": "2026-11-24T10:07:11.000Z",
          "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50626099",
          "textZhHtml": "This is the age old prescriptivism vs descriptivism issue. I understood the meaning here and I suspect most others did too. From a descriptivist point of view that makes this meaning legitimate."
        },
        {
          "id": 50622538,
          "author": "icyfox",
          "publishedAt": "2026-11-24T01:57:59.000Z",
          "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50622538",
          "textZhHtml": "As literal as you can imagine"
        },
